	IMO 5% is probably about as high as we want it to be!  It's true
that the odds of an instakill on any one hit isn't very high, but I
think Vorpal Blade is a net positive as long as it allows you to kill
things faster than you would have otherwise.

	Look at it this way: your chance of _not_ beheading something each
hit is 95%.  Therefore your chance of not having beheaded it after two
hits is .95^2 or 0.9025.  Within five hits, there's roughly a 25% chance
that one of them has been a beheading stroke.  (Or, put a different way,
there's only a ~75% chance that the fight could even last that long,
regular damage aside.)

	If we upped the "vorpal percentage" to 10%, you'd have a roughly 40%
chance of an instakill within five hits!  I think that's a bit much.

